course: dictionary
lesson: 11704
title: Audible: what we can hear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Audible means loud enough to be heard. If your ears can pick up a sound, it is audible. If it is too quiet, too high or too far away, it is not audible.
explain: «The ticking clock was barely audible in the quiet room.» Barely tells you the sound was only just loud enough to hear. So audible is about how loud a sound is, not how nice it sounds.
explain: In science lessons on sound, we say a sound is audible when our ears can detect it. Some sounds are too high or too low to be audible to people, even though they are really there.
fact: «Audible» means loud enough to be heard.
fact: «Barely audible» means only just loud enough to hear.
fact: «Clearly audible» means easy to hear.
fact: Ultrasound is sound too high to be audible to human ears.
fact: «Audible» is an adjective, and its adverb is «audibly», as in «She spoke audibly.»
exercise: «The bell was clearly audible from the far end of the playground.» What does audible mean? | Very fast | *Loud enough to be heard | Hidden out of sight | Sweet and gentle
exercise: Why is ultrasound not audible to most people? | It is always silent | It is too slow to notice | *It is too high for human ears to hear | It is too quiet to see
exercise: «The ticking clock was barely audible in the quiet room.» What does barely audible mean? | Loud enough to shake the walls | *Only just loud enough to hear | Not there at all, like a silent ghost | Painted in bright colours
test: «The music was audible through the wall.» Find and copy the word that means loud enough to be heard. | wall | *audible | through | music
test: Which word is the adverb form of audible? | *audibly | loudly | audible | audio
exam: «The whisper was barely audible, so Ruby leaned closer.» What does barely audible mean? | *Only just loud enough to hear | Written down in a book | Very rude and unfriendly | Loud enough to hear from across the street
